====================================================================
BLENDER VERSION COMPATIBILITY
====================================================================

NEVER assume the newest Blender API.

Before using version-sensitive APIs:

- inspect capabilities at runtime
- use safe fallbacks
- avoid unsupported enum values
- avoid unsupported properties
- avoid version-specific assumptions

Especially check:

- render engines
- Eevee
- Cycles
- Workbench
- modifiers
- bevel
- normals
- UV APIs
- BMesh operators
- Geometry Nodes APIs
- shader socket names
- color management
- animation APIs
- collection APIs

Example logic:

if modern Eevee exists:
    use it

elif compatible legacy Eevee exists:
    use it

elif Cycles exists:
    use Cycles

else:
    use the safest available fallback

The exact code must be adapted to the actual Blender API.

